00:19:33.234 --> 00:19:34.650
And one of the
most exciting parts

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:37.386
was hearing Matz, the
creator of Ruby, speak.

00:19:37.386 --> 00:19:38.760
And he was talking
about how Ruby

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:40.110
is becoming a mature language.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:43.230
I mean, I got involved back
when it was, I think, Ruby 1.8.

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:47.400
And I've been through 1.9, and
we're on to 2.3 at this point.

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:49.440
And the planning now is
going on for Ruby 3.0.

00:19:49.440 --> 00:19:50.898
And there's a lot
of talk about how

00:19:50.898 --> 00:19:52.255
to support concurrency well.

00:19:52.255 --> 00:19:54.630
There's a lot of talk about
improving performance, making

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:56.520
Ruby three times faster.

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:58.830
And I'm glad that those
conversations are happening.

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:01.920
And they're raising some
interesting questions

00:20:01.920 --> 00:20:03.326
about language design.

00:20:03.326 --> 00:20:05.700
Because one of Ruby's guiding
principles has always been,

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:09.660
it needs to be easy and
delightful for the programmer.

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:11.250
But that means there's
some stuff that

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:12.660
maybe isn't so
easy or delightful

00:20:12.660 --> 00:20:15.481
for the actual computer.

00:20:15.481 --> 00:20:16.980
For example, all
the metaprogramming

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:18.570
that's really easy
to do in Ruby,

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:20.445
I was talking to someone
today about the fact

00:20:20.445 --> 00:20:24.060
that in Rails you might
be debugging methods

00:20:24.060 --> 00:20:26.970
that don't exist
on in the source

00:20:26.970 --> 00:20:29.970
because they're dynamically
created at runtime.

00:20:29.970 --> 00:20:32.530
And that makes some
things very hard.

00:20:32.530 --> 00:20:33.870
And so talking about that.

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:35.050
And I'm really excited
where that's going.

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:37.130
I'm also-- it's also excited
to see just who was there.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.588
It was a lot of
folks there talking

00:20:38.588 --> 00:20:41.257
